>
> This solution for NIMBLE is the same as I use in R, so I don't loose anything switching to NIMBLE here. I'm just wondering if there is a way to leverage NIMBLE functionality so that the user does not need to be an expert on activity center mixing in these models. The only idea I have is perhaps NIMBLE can tune 2 proposal parameters for you in a custom update and you apply one to the situation where z[i]=1 and sum(y[i,]=0) and another to the situation where z[i]=1 and sum(y[i,]>0). z[i]=0 are then proposed from the prior. It seems unlikely this would be possible, but who knows!
