HI all,

I'm building a model with a spatial hierarchy: all LSOAs fit inside a unique LAD. The model is as follows

code <- nimbleCode({
# PRIORS

# COMMON TERMS
alpha0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.00001)
beta0 ~ dnorm(0, 0.00001)
# AREA TERMS -- random effects for intercepts and slopes
# LAD terms
for(j_LAD in 1:N_LAD){
alpha_LAD[j_LAD] ~ dnorm(alpha0, tau_alpha_LAD) # centred on common terms
beta_LAD[j_LAD] ~ dnorm(beta0, tau_beta_LAD)
}
sigma_alpha_LAD ~ dunif(0,2)
tau_alpha_LAD <- pow(sigma_alpha_LAD,-2)
sigma_beta_LAD ~ dunif(0,2)
tau_beta_LAD <- pow(sigma_beta_LAD,-2)

# LSOA terms
for(j in 1:N_LSOA){
id_LAD <- filter(mortality_m, LSOA.id == j)$LAD.id[1] # picks out LAD for jth LSOA
alpha1[j] ~ dnorm(alpha_LAD[id_LAD], tau_alpha1) # centred on LAD terms
beta1[j] ~ dnorm(beta_LAD[id_LAD], tau_beta1)
}
sigma_alpha1 ~ dunif(0,2)
tau_alpha1 <- pow(sigma_alpha1,-2)
sigma_beta1 ~ dunif(0,2)
tau_beta1 <- pow(sigma_beta1,-2)

# Put all parameters together into indexed lograte
for(a in 1:N_age_groups){
for(j in 1:N_LSOA){
for(t in 1:N_year){
lograte[a, j, t] <- alpha1[j] + beta1[j] * (t - 8)
}
}
}

# LIKELIHOOD
# N total number of cells, i.e. ages*years*areas(*sex)
for (i in 1:N) {
# y is number of deaths in that cell, assumed Poisson
# mu is predicted number of deaths in that cell
y[i] ~ dpois(mu[i])
log(mu[i]) <- log(n[i]) + lograte[age[i], LSOA[i], yr[i]]
}
})

Currently I'm using dplyr's filter method to pick out the right LAD corresponding to the LSOA in that loop (nimble did not like [, ] slicing), but I get the following error:

Error in getSymbolicParentNodesRecurse(x, constNames, indexNames, nimbleFunctionNames,  :
  R function 'filter' has arguments that cannot be evaluated; either the function must be a nimbleFunction or values for the following inputs must be specified as constants in the model: mortality_m,LSOA.id.

Is there a quick workaround for what seems a fairly straightforward problem of calling the LAD that the LSOA lies within?

Best,

Theo

