One possible solution, if I understand your question correctly, would be to use a "grid lookup" type approach.

Give nimble a data object with id_LADs and have it pull from that.  For instance, the object grid.lookup could be a N_LAD X N_LSOA matrix with each entry representing the id for that LAD/LSOA combo. You could then call:

alpha1[J_LAD,j] ~ dnorm(alpha_LAD[grid.lookup[j_LAD,j]], tau_alpha1) or similar.

