Thanks for the good answer.  We sometimes refer to that as "nested indexing", but "grid lookup" also makes sense.

Small technical note:  It is better to provide id_LADs as constants rather than data.  However, a relatively recent internal feature is that we attempt to check if a vector provided as data is actually used as a constant indexing vector and if so to treat it like part of constants.  So, as long as that feature works, it shouldn't matter anymore, but still one might argue there is a conceptual clarity in providing it as constants.

-Perry

